Fixed. The bug: in `ExternalGlob::expand_glob` (crates/nu-command/src/system/run_external.rs:334), a bare `.` argument is glob-expanded to the cwd itself, and `strip_prefix(cwd)` then produced an empty string, which git rejects as an invalid pathspec.

The fix returns `.` instead of an empty string when stripping PWD results in an empty path:

```rust
let path_stripped = if self.strip_working_directory {
    match path.strip_prefix(cwd) {
        // If stripping PWD results in an empty path, return `.` instead.
        Ok(remainder) if remainder.as_os_str().is_empty() => Path::new("."),
        Ok(remainder) => remainder,
        Err(_) => &path,
    }
} else {
    &path
};
```

